# Runbooks

This directory contains static, project-owned operation documentation subordinate to [`../OPERATIONS.md`](../OPERATIONS.md). A runbook explains a reviewed procedure and its evidence; it is not an executor, command registry, hook, scheduler, or permission-bearing configuration.

## Generation boundary

Only one complete, unique, user-confirmed strict structured procedure record in `Confirmed` can produce a deterministic ordinary Markdown file at `docs/runbooks/<slug>.md`. The record must contain exactly these nine fields:

- `slug`
- `title`
- `trigger`
- `reads`
- `actions`
- `stop_conditions`
- `evidence`
- `permissions`
- `rollback`

All nine fields are required. No aliases, additional fields, values, or defaults are accepted or inferred. Incomplete, malformed, generic, inferred, Proposed, Open, Sources-only, or duplicate records produce no runbook.

Generated runbooks contain no frontmatter, executor metadata, hooks, command registration, shell metadata, tool permissions, or other privilege-bearing configuration. They are ordinary Markdown and remain useful after setup without a package or target runtime. Project and host owners perform any actual command execution, Agent dispatch, deployment, publication, signing, or external action.

No generated authority directs an Agent to locate, install, resolve, import, invoke, or verify Reporivet or a package diagnosis command. Do not infer or execute a procedure from a partial record, a generic note, a filename, a marker, or a location.

